<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭ-nūdus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>half-naked</i> (not ante-Aug.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">consules, prope seminudi sub jugum missi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 9,
					6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">24, 40</span></i>; 
			<i><span class="en">Suet. Vit. 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Front. Princ. Hist. p.
			318</span></i>.—As <i>subst.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ille seminudus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ep. 6, 2, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>half-unarmed</i>,
				<i>almost defenceless</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedes vagus et prope seminudus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					31, 35, 6</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sententiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Front. Ep. ad Anton. 1, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
